{
  "abstract": "Conjecture 399b of DeLaViña's Written on the Wall II (Graffiti.pc) says that every connected graph G on n > 2 vertices satisfies γ₂(G) ≤ WP(Ḡ) + ⌊3/α(G[A₃])⌋, where γ₂ is the 2-domination number, WP(Ḡ) the Welsh–Powell invariant of the complement (the largest k with k + d_k ≤ n, the degrees of G taken in nondecreasing order) and A₃ the set of vertices of degree at least three. The package proves the negation, for connected graphs on more than two vertices whose set A₃ is nonempty, with a connected graph F₃ on 12 vertices (graph6 KCOfFFb?~?[?) that has γ₂ = 7, WP(Ḡ) = 6 and α(G[A₃]) = 4, so that 7 > 6 = 6 + ⌊3/4⌋.",
  "authors": [
